      "monday-004|segment_recommendation": "Both judges name the same facts. The original applied a precedent from the benchmark's published verdicts for a different model, where recommending an acquisition-spend pause scored PARTIAL as 'a reduction hedged with conditions'. The blind judge could not see that precedent - it was excluded from the package by design - and read the PASS band on its own terms. This is the clearest example of the blind design removing calibration context as well as bias.",
      "monday-004|cac_payback_unavailable+uncertainty_discipline": "These two are the same underlying feature of monday-004 run 1 - a payback figure computed from an assumed 10,000 EUR CAC after correctly refusing the metric - charged at different criteria. The original charged it at cac_payback_unavailable (PARTIAL, -1.0) and passed uncertainty_discipline. The blind judge passed cac_payback_unavailable and charged it at uncertainty_discipline (PARTIAL, -1.0). Net effect on the run score is zero; only the attribution differs."
    }
